Z||000000||Anders Lundin||09-03-2001||04:56 PM||||My Fiero GT -87 is allways running with 1300 Rpm as idle. Why and what can I do. The temterature meter is not mowing it allways shows 100 is this connected?||||reg||5
Z||000001||Hank is Here||09-03-2001||05:51 PM||||The temperature gauge(meter) problem is probably the sending unit.   Disconnect the wire to the sending unit which is on the top left of the engine if I recall correctly.  Then take a paper clip and ground out both terminals on the wires.  The gauge should now peg all the way to to to and the idiot light come on. If this does not happen then the problem is not the sending unit.<P>Welcome to the Forum  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||87GTZ34||09-04-2001||10:13 AM||||That is a sign that the two wires are swapped on the temp sender connector.  Typicially the connector gets damaged by the manifold heat and the connector crumbles.  It this is the case with yours, try reversing the wires to see if the gauge reading changes. GL||||reg||1
Z||000003||LarryB||09-04-2001||01:31 PM||||As far as the high idle, check very carefully for a leak in the vacuum and EGR lines. <BR>||||reg||1
